Old Samurai
~ samurai_start
Old Samurai (without turning, calm): You walk like someone who has forgotten how to fear pain.
- Are you the healer? => samurai_observe
- I was told you could help me. => samurai_observe
- …(silent) => samurai_observe

~ samurai_observe
Old Samurai (turns slowly, eyes sharp): Help is never simple. Sit. Let me look at that wound.
- I don’t trust healers. => samurai_trust
- Do what you must. => samurai_trust
- …(silent) => samurai_trust

~ samurai_trust
Old Samurai (examining the armor): This steel… I know it. Black Crescent craftsmanship. Efficient. Cruel.
- I didn’t choose this armor. => samurai_memory
- It was given to me. => samurai_memory

~ samurai_memory
Old Samurai (snorts quietly): Armor is never “given.” It is worn willingly… or after something is taken from you.
(pause)
You don’t remember, do you?
- No. => samurai_reveal
- I remember fragments. Blood. Orders. => samurai_reveal

~ samurai_reveal
Old Samurai (nods slowly): Then you are more dangerous than you know. A blade without memory still cuts true.
- Will you heal me? => samurai_choice
- Why do you help someone like me? => samurai_choice

~ samurai_choice
Old Samurai (turns away, preparing herbs): I do not heal soldiers. I heal consequences.
The Crescent left scars on this land… and on you.
- You sound like you know them well. => samurai_past
- I don’t want to be their weapon anymore. => samurai_past

~ samurai_past
Old Samurai (voice low): Once, they came to my village. Asked for obedience. Took children to “train.”
I refused. They burned everything but this place.
- Why didn’t they kill you? => samurai_reason
- I’m sorry. => samurai_reason

~ samurai_reason
Old Samurai (meets your eyes): Because I killed their captain.
Since then, I heal those they break… and wait.
- Wait for what? => samurai_truth
- For revenge? => samurai_truth

~ samurai_truth
Old Samurai (quiet, steady): For the moment when their strongest knight forgets who he was…
and must decide who he will become.
- Are you talking about me? => samurai_decision

~ samurai_decision
Old Samurai (placing a hand on your shoulder): The wound will close. The pain will fade.
But memory… memory returns only when you are ready to face it.
- Then heal me. => samurai_heal
- I’m afraid of what I’ll remember. => samurai_heal

~ samurai_heal
Old Samurai (beginning the ritual): Fear is good. It means you are still human.
(pause)
When the Crescent comes for you again… remember this:
You were not born a monster.
- I’ll remember. => samurai_end
- …(silent) => samurai_end

~ samurai_end
Old Samurai: Rest here tonight. At dawn, the road will open.

- Rest 
do GameState.change_night.emit()

Old Samurai: [wait=5] I did everything I could. 
Now it is up to you. What you choose to do with your sword… is no longer their decision.
=> END